  /* safety */
  "safety.aFitnessAppHolds": "A fitness app holds two kinds of information that matter: what your body is doing, and what your body can't safely do. This page says what we do with both, in plain terms rather than by reference to a policy document.",
  "safety.aPausedPlan": "A paused plan",
  "safety.aPersonAtFynrox": "A person at Fynrox reviews serious flags, and a professional working with you is expected to escalate rather than coach through something clinical. Escalating is the correct behaviour here, not a failure.",
  "safety.aWarningBeforeThe": "A warning before the session",
  "safety.anEscalation": "An escalation",
  "safety.andGivesNoMedical": "<strong>Fynrox is not a medical device</strong> and gives no medical advice, diagnosis or treatment. Nothing in the app, including Fynrox AI and a Fynrox professional, replaces a clinician who can examine you. If you're unwell, or something hurts in a way that worries you, that conversation comes first.",
  "safety.bothAreRequestsYou": "Both are requests you make from inside the app, and both have a status you can watch rather than an email you hope arrives. An export produces a file you can download for a limited window. A deletion is scheduled rather than instant, so you have a window to cancel it if it was a mistake or wasn't you — after that it runs and it isn't recoverable.",
  "safety.contactUs": "Contact us",
  "safety.countsNeverPeopleHow": "<strong>Your gym or the creator who referred you.</strong> Counts, never people. How many members they introduced and how many activated — not who trained what, not your weight, not your health screen. That boundary is enforced in the API, so a partner portal cannot ask for an individual's data even by accident.",
  "safety.encryptedAndKeptApart": "Encrypted, and kept apart",
  "safety.everythingYourTrainingLog": "<strong>You.</strong> Everything. Your training log, meals, recovery check-ins, progress photos, conversations with Fynrox AI, and the health notes you entered at onboarding.",
  "safety.exportItOrDelete": "Export it, or delete it",
  "safety.forAnythingThatShouldnt": "For anything that shouldn't be trained through until a professional has looked at it. A declared heart condition always pauses the plan. The pause can't be talked out of by the AI coach — that's the point of it.",
  "safety.forThingsThatChange": "For things that change how you should train rather than whether you should — a recent injury, a joint that's been flaring. You see it before you start, not buried in a settings screen you'll never open.",
  "safety.healthData": "HEALTH DATA",
  "safety.metaDescription": "What Fynrox does with health data, when it stops you training rather than encouraging you, what partners can and cannot see, and how to export or delete your data.",
  "safety.metaOgDescription": "What we do with health data, and when the app stops you rather than encouraging you.",
  "safety.metaOgTitle": "Safety & privacy — Fynrox",
  "safety.onboardingIncludesAShort": "Onboarding includes a short health screen, and the weekly check-in can raise the same flags later. What happens next depends on what was raised:",
  "safety.onlyTheRolesWhose": "<strong>Fynrox staff.</strong> Only the roles whose job requires it, and access to sensitive data is logged with who looked and why.",
  "safety.onlyWhatYouAgreed": "<strong>A professional you've accepted.</strong> Only what you agreed to share, shown to you as a list before the relationship starts, and only while it's active. Ending the relationship ends their access the same day — enforced on our side, not by asking them to stop looking. They never see your payment details or your AI conversations.",
  "safety.pageTitle": "Safety & privacy — Fynrox",
  "safety.privacy": "PRIVACY",
  "safety.readBeforeYouSign": "Read before you sign up",
  "safety.safety": "SAFETY",
  "safety.safetyPrivacy": "SAFETY & PRIVACY",
  "safety.somethingHereYouWant": "Something here you want to ask about?",
  "safety.theConditionsAndInjuries": "The conditions and injuries you declare are encrypted at rest with a key the application holds, separately from the rest of your profile. They exist so the app can keep you away from movements that would hurt you — not to be a field anyone browses. They are not part of what a professional sees when you start working together, and they are never shared with a partner.",
  "safety.theFullLegalText": "The full legal text is in the <a href=\"/privacy.html\">privacy policy</a> and the <a href=\"/terms.html\">terms of service</a>. Both are in review before general availability; this page describes what the software actually does today.",
  "safety.theTwoThingsWorth": "The two things worth being specific about.",
  "safety.whenTheAppStops": "When the app stops you",
  "safety.whoCanSeeWhat": "Who can see what",
  "safety.yourRights": "YOUR RIGHTS",

